The instrument predated INV-karud's situation collapse, so it reported one unit
while calling it the other: an evidence record has been a SITUATION since the
collapse, standing for `collapsed_flow_count` source->sink PAIRS, and the
script kept only the witness scalars. Three changes:

* `collapsed_flow_count` / `source_primitives` / `sink_primitives` /
  `sink_symbols` reach every flow row. Absent -> 1, so 0001 and 0003 flow files
  still score correctly: there, one record WAS one pair.
* `score` prints a per-situation and a per-row rate side by side in every
  table, and REFUSES (exit 1, offending ids named) to print a row rate for a
  multi-pair TP carrying no `tp_pairs`. A situation is TP iff AT LEAST ONE of
  its pairs is, so "all" inflates and "one" deflates. `unadj_pairs` exists so a
  situation-unit run reconciles with a pair-unit run instead of folding those
  rows into FP.
* `collect --no-collapse` rebinds `taint.collapse_unadjudicated_flows` to the
  identity for that process only, so the row unit is ADJUDICATED on its own
  records rather than apportioned. 0004 had to hand-block that. Production is
  untouched and `collect` prints which arm it ran.

Measurement 0005 (census of 0004's five-repo cohort at ba01153095):
21.6% per situation (8 TP of 37), 10.0% per row (17 TP of 170), a 2.16x gap.
Positive control first: 0 CONFIRMED verdicts anywhere -- 13 violated, 22
inconclusive.

The two collect arms reconcile exactly -- 37 situations summing to 170 pairs
against 170 pair records, every member set recovered (37/37), both ledgers
agreeing on TP=17, FP=153.

WI-sivuz's pre-registered adversarial control was run on the owner's explicit
authorisation. Four blind adjudicators over disjoint chunks: 0.0% disagreement
over all 37. And then the two passes that followed changed the headline TWICE,
in opposite directions -- an adjudication overturned the one contested label
(row 7.9% -> 10.6%) and an adversarial refuter broke 1 of the 9 true positives
(situation 24.3% -> 21.6%, row -> 10.0%). 0001's caveat is not a formality: a
zero disagreement rate shows the rubric was applied consistently, not that it
is right.

The 297 -> 170 row drop is one scope decision, not a precision fix. Re-running
the identical census with two scope-probe claims added restores 0004's
population repo for repo (caddy 219, mitmproxy 60, poetry 13, express 3,
apollo-server 2), and the 170 rows are a strict subset by flow identity.

No band movement is claimed. WI-sivuz's bands were named before any interval
was computed; this is input to the owner's re-rank, which gates INV-linub.

